1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:12,910
Hello! In this short video, let us look at the new filters on the Orders page of the Qwipo Seller Store. These filters help you find and plan your orders quickly.

2
00:00:14,310 --> 00:00:25,970
This is the Orders page. At the top are the status tabs. Below them, you can see the totals, then the new filters, and then the search bar.

3
00:00:27,370 --> 00:00:39,200
The status tabs show All, New, Confirmed, Logistics, Delivered and Cancelled orders. The number on each tab tells you how many orders are in it.

4
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:50,750
This line shows the number of customers, the number of orders, and the total order value. It changes every time you apply a filter.

5
00:00:52,150 --> 00:01:05,280
This is the new Delivery Day filter. You can see All Days, and every day of the week, from Monday to Sunday. The number shows how many orders are delivered on that day.

6
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:21,580
When you click a day, like Monday, a new row opens with the real dates. For example, Monday the fifth of October, and Monday the twelfth of October. Orders from all Mondays are shown together.

7
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:31,040
Click a date to see only the orders for that date. Click the same date again to go back to all Mondays.

8
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:43,960
Next is the Order Type filter. You can choose All, Beat orders, or Non-beat orders. Here, we are seeing only the non-beat orders.

9
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:57,000
You can use the filters together. Here we picked Saturday, the tenth of October, and Beat orders. Now we see only the beat orders for that date.

10
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:08,940
Notice that the numbers on the status tabs also change. So you can quickly see how many of these orders are new, confirmed, or delivered.

11
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:21,000
Open the New tab to see only the new orders for your filters. You can select orders here, and confirm or cancel them, just like before.

12
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:30,940
The search bar is just below the filters. Type an order ID or a retailer name to find an order quickly.

13
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:36,920
To remove all the filters at once, click Clear filters.

14
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:48,930
If a new order is waiting for a long time, you will see a label like, three days pending. This reminds you to confirm or cancel that order.

15
00:02:50,330 --> 00:03:00,460
That's all! Use the Delivery Day, Dates and Order Type filters to plan your deliveries easily. Thank you for watching.
